	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13993"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=994" title="View the profile of Prodigy">Prodigy</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 20<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=994"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:jroge15@lsu.edu"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13993#msg13993"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg13993#msg13993">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #22 on:</b> January 27, 2005, 03:09:53 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Always sad to see a guild go, and one being as well known as Ascent brings a shockwave to the entire server.&nbsp; You have seen changes happening for the last couple of monthes, with guilds disbanding, high end characters selling and moving on.&nbsp; However, nothing is more shocking than to hear of Ascent disbanding.&nbsp; I use to admire you guys.&nbsp; Ya&#039;ll were great people, very friendly. (most anyway) Until drama queens moved in, and ruined the fun for the old core people which I am assuming made more people leave.&nbsp; Makes you wanna stab someone in the eye. <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/devil1.gif" alt="Devil" border="0" />&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/banghead2.gif" alt="banghead2" border="0" /><br /><br />Zilk, Shib.&nbsp; Best of luck in wherever you go.&nbsp; As for the rest of ya&#039;ll /hats off and best of luck.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14002"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 139<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14002#msg14002"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14002#msg14002">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #23 on:</b> January 27, 2005, 07:16:24 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I definitely wouldn&#039;t call the guild dead, and I rather dislike hearing comments to that regard here :P&nbsp; &nbsp;We almost guilddeleted I think three times. First when me, Vesi, Reia, Brae etc left for WoW beta, essentially taking about 80% of the people who had seen NToV, Ssra Emp etc with Ascent. Then again when Honch quit soon after. There was one more round of consideration iirc, but they tried staying around.<br /><br />I don&#039;t know exactly what happened online except that Garadan had RL intervening which dropped it all on Ssnakess, who ended up getting more pissed than entertained by that, and hence decided to migrate to join the guild core in WoW. Then it was rolled on to Fysts, who decided to stop holding off the inevitable I guess. There are very few older members remaining in Ascent EQ... Of the core that visited Las Vegas back when, the only ones remaining are Fysts, Vayanla and Cartier, unless I missed someone. Old 50% attendees I can see are limited to Aellis, Fysts and Vay. Some of the remaining core are following the main core finally, others just can&#039;t let go and are switching servers to join another uberguild - - <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Ya&#039;ll were great people, very friendly. (most anyway) Until drama queens moved in, and ruined the fun for the old core people which I am assuming made more people leave.&nbsp; </div>The old core people leaving had nothing to do with drama queens. It had lot to do with shit like Uqua, Rathe etc, and just knowing the game way too well to have any sense of newness in it.<br /><br /><br />As for Kinladars comment... Ascent just is a raiding guild. We&#039;re defined by the fact that we do the high end content. We have too many people who get bored to tears without that element to the game, and adding people like Dyvim to the old core just made that so much more acute. If we do not do the higher end content, there is no reason for us to play.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14005"></a>
