	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14009"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=321" title="View the profile of Garadan">Garadan</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 45<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/bartmoon.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Fuck you, I know I&#039;m a asshole<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=321"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:GaradanR@netscape.net"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14009#msg14009"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14009#msg14009">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #26 on:</b> January 27, 2005, 10:25:02 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I jump in iirc every once in awhile, although your probably sleeping when I do Del. I am moving to germany because of military, we (my wife) got orders there. So we will have a 3 year tour there. I have considered rolling to WoW but atm really isnt a good idea with so much going on before I leave for Germany. <br /><br />As for Ascent, we were going strong up until basically Christmas. Anguish was two raids away. Once the new year hit I had a ton of shit come up irl that really needed my full attention. Ssnakess/Karadana said from the begining that they didnt want to be leaders in the sense of leading the guild. They stuck around more or less out of friendship to me to help me out. So when I wasnt online 9 times out of 10 they werent either. Fysts really tried to step it up and take control of things when I was gone. But the problem is, with every change in leadership there are those that test the capabilities of said leader. So what was going semi smooth during me being around, changed when I dissappeared. When Honch quit and I took over, the same shit happened. I had to basically lay down the law and be a real asshole to start weeding out those that were gonna follow and those that couldnt (ie Rogosh, Galamir, and whatever that retarded rangers name was that came from forsaken... started with a K ) <br /><br />The guild is breaking up strictly because the core of old school ascent is gone. The few of us that remained like Cartier, Fysts, Baelt, Vayanla, Aellis etc are either quiting or transfering. I&#039;m done with EQ. Shit I was done with it almost a year ago when I left then. When I came back just to see what was going on, Delheru and 70% of the guild had all went to Wow. Just Honch and a few other orginal members were still around. I only stayed playing due to Karadana talking me into it, which eventually ended up with me taking over the guild. But I have to say I am thankful and proud for those that stuck it out and busted ass for me and the guild. When I came back the guild was pretty much dead, after months of hard ass work we climbed back up to the #2 spot and really could of kept going but rl is a bitch. The breaking up of Ascent in EQ has nothing to do with drama at all. Any high end raiding guild knows there is always drama. Thats what happens when you start racing and clashing for mobs to kill. Just think of it as a little extra political fun on top of killing high end mobs.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=335131" target="_blank"><img src="http://www2.freepichosting.com/Images/421460356/4.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
